  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4dc5331b40204628afa94f7e24f8e5c2, type: 3}
  m_Name: Tycoon Vanderbilt
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ScriptableObjects.TrueEncounterData
  vendorName: Tycoon Vanderbilt
  offerText: Fund my transcontinental railroad project today. It demands a staggering
    amount of your capital, and you must store these massive iron prototypes, but
    the dividends will secure your legacy forever.
  acceptResultText: You hand over a small fortune. The giant, rusting iron prototypes
    completely ruin your floor space. As Vanderbilt walks away smiling, a terrifying
    sense of dread washes over you.
  rejectResultText: You flatly refuse to fund his overly ambitious, suspicious project.
    Keeping your massive fortune safely locked away feels incredibly smart.
  acceptedDelayedText: 'The news finally hits: Vanderbilt''s railroad was a colossal
    Ponzi scheme! The authorities ruthlessly seize your remaining assets to cover
    his debts, and the crushing shock gives you a near-fatal heart attack.'
  rejectedDelayedText: Vanderbilt's empire officially collapses in a historic, city-wide
    scandal! Because you kept your capital safe, you effortlessly buy out all of
    his bankrupt competitors for mere pennies, becoming a true market king!
  accepted: 0
  rejectedEffects:
